# Claude Skills in This Repo

This repo includes **Claude skills** in `.claude/skills/`. Cursor loads them for compatibility; they are also symlinked under `.cursor/skills/` for discovery.

## When to Use a Skill

When the user's task matches a skill's trigger (e.g. Word docs, PDFs, spreadsheets, frontend design, presentations, proofreading, LaTeX compile, R review), **read the full skill** and follow it:

1. **Identify the skill** — Match the task to a skill in `.claude/skills/` (or `.cursor/skills/`).
2. **Read the skill file** — Open `.claude/skills/<skill-name>/SKILL.md` (or the same under `.cursor/skills/`) and follow its instructions.
3. **Apply the skill** — Use any scripts, references, or assets the skill specifies.

## Skills in This Repo (.claude/skills/)

| Category | Skills (examples) |
|----------|-------------------|
| Documents | docx, pdf, pptx, xlsx |
| Design / UI | frontend-design, theme-factory, canvas-design, algorithmic-art, brand-guidelines |
| Workflow | doc-coauthoring, internal-comms, skill-creator, mcp-builder, humanizer |
| Research / LaTeX | compile-latex, proofread, review-r, validate-bib, lit-review, research-ideation, review-paper, data-analysis |
| Other | webapp-testing, web-artifacts-builder, slack-gif-creator |

If a task clearly fits a skill's "Use when..." description, read that skill's `SKILL.md` and follow it before implementing.
